1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,545
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:05,463
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,885
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:12,929
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,227
[Dmitri] <i>You won't get</i>
<i>your father back if you kill Red.</i>

7
00:00:19,310 --> 00:00:20,895
[Audrey screams, in English] <i>Dad! Dad!</i>

8
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:21,938
[Martina, in English] <i>Oh my God.</i>

9
00:00:22,021 --> 00:00:23,523
[Martina, in English] <i>You know,</i>
<i>this is all Atoy's fault,</i>

10
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:24,941
<i>but this is also on you!</i>

11
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:28,194
This wouldn't have happened if Red
hadn't done something to Atoy's father!

12
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:30,613
For once, side with your own family!

13
00:00:31,573 --> 00:00:34,868
Tatoy, what happened to your hand?

14
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:38,204
[Audrey] <i>Did Atoy</i>
<i>really mean to shoot you?</i>

15
00:00:38,288 --> 00:00:39,539
[in English] Yes, he did.

16
00:00:39,622 --> 00:00:41,332
He's not that kind of person, Dad.

17
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:43,668
[Karla] <i>He even forbade Gavin</i>
<i>from being friends with me.</i>

18
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:46,171
- [Emerson] <i>Gavin Regalia, Red's son?</i>
- [Karla] <i>Yes.</i>

19
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:49,340
Karla, Gavin's father was the one
who hit-and-run Sir Delfin.

20
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,675
What?

21
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:54,137
How can I tell our child
that you almost killed her grandfather?!

22
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,639
Will we be safe with you?!

23
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:59,017
[Gavin, in English] <i>He asked me</i>
<i>where my Dad was last night.</i>

24
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,393
Turns out he already had--

25
00:01:00,477 --> 00:01:01,895
had something bad planned for Dad.

26
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:05,190
I just really wanted to have
a happy and complete family.

27
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:08,943
I thought it would happen
when Audrey and Janine were given to me.

28
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:11,154
We're still here, Tatoy.

29
00:01:11,237 --> 00:01:14,532
[Ibyang] <i>We may not be blood-related, but…</i>

30
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:16,034
<i>we're still your family.</i>

31
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:18,578
<i>We're not a drawing that can be erased.</i>

32
00:01:18,661 --> 00:01:20,538
Brother, sorry if I haven't
been around lately.

33
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:22,499
[Karla] <i>Sorry if I've been stubborn.</i>

34
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:23,792
‪PREVIOUSLY

35
00:01:33,676 --> 00:01:35,845
[music fades]

36
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:39,432
[softly] Thank you.

37
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,978
[utensils clattering]

38
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:49,150
Karla, thank you for what you did earlier.

39
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:51,444
Atoy appreciated that you were there.

40
00:01:51,528 --> 00:01:53,571
Especially now that
he's going through something.

41
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:56,574
Mom, I did not apologize to Brother Atoy

42
00:01:56,658 --> 00:01:58,368
because I was stubborn.

43
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:02,914
I apologized because he thinks
we're honest with him, but…

44
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,749
we're not.

45
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:07,752
He doesn't need to know that.

46
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:10,672
Karla, I hope

47
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:12,924
you trust me.

48
00:02:13,424 --> 00:02:15,718
I hope you'll tell me everything too.

49
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:19,389
Mom, what else should I say to you?

50
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:22,433
The man who brought you home,

51
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:23,852
is he your boyfriend now?

52
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:25,478
Gavin?

53
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:26,563
Oh, no.

54
00:02:27,647 --> 00:02:30,817
Ah, he looks kind and trustworthy.

55
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,777
Invite him to dinner here sometime,

56
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:36,364
I'll cook for him,
as a thank you for bringing you home.

57
00:02:37,365 --> 00:02:40,952
Mom, I don't know
if we'll still be friends.

58
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:42,871
Hmm? Why not?

59
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:45,874
Mom, his father killed my father,

60
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:48,585
Sir Delfin.

61
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:51,045
He's Red Regalia's son.

62
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:56,050
That's why I don't know
if we'll still be friends,

63
00:02:56,634 --> 00:02:57,969
even if I want to.

64
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:01,055
[suspicious music playing]

65
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,353
[music fades]

66
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:08,563
[Gavin] Karla.

67
00:03:08,646 --> 00:03:09,814
Gavin.

68
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:11,399
How are you?

69
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:13,693
Wait, let me just get your jacket.

70
00:03:15,361 --> 00:03:16,696
Karla, wait.

71
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:19,115
Did you hurt Cathy?

72
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:22,410
We fought, but she started it.

73
00:03:23,494 --> 00:03:25,788
You really take after
your Brother Atoy, huh?

74
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:27,373
You're hot-headed too.

75
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:30,335
Why is Brother Atoy involved?

76
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:32,962
Don't tell me you don't know what he did?

77
00:03:33,046 --> 00:03:34,881
He shot my grandfather.

78
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:36,883
He beat up my father!

79
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:38,676
He's lucky my grandfather
won't press charges

80
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,261
because he's thinking of Janine!

81
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:41,387
Why?

82
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:44,432
Your father deserved it!

83
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:47,477
He killed Sir Delfin,
Brother Atoy's and my father!

84
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:50,146
What evidence does your brother have
to accuse him, huh?

85
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:54,609
Did he see my dad himself?
Did he see him commit the hit-and-run?!

86
00:03:54,692 --> 00:03:56,194
Or maybe he's just looking for trouble!

87
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:58,696
You don't know Brother Atoy!
He's not like your father!

88
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,323
Your brother isn't a saint!

89
00:04:00,406 --> 00:04:03,701
Okay? He's just like your father!
They're both pretenders!

90
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:06,120
What you're saying is foul!

91
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:09,749
Don't drag my father into this. He's dead!

92
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:12,293
And he was killed by your criminal father!

93
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:15,838
I wish I hadn't told you my problems,

94
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:17,799
if you'd just use them against me!

95
00:04:17,882 --> 00:04:20,093
[tense music playing]

96
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:21,678
Leave now!

97
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:23,179
Get out! Out!

98
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:25,014
Leave!

99
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:27,892
[sobbing]

100
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:41,030
[suave theme music playing]

101
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:14,022
But, miss, do you think

102
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:16,441
Atoy and Audrey broke up?

103
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:21,154
That's the vibe I got last night.

104
00:05:21,237 --> 00:05:23,197
I just feel sad for Atoy

105
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:25,575
because neither of them
wants this situation.

106
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:28,828
Maybe they're really not meant to be.

107
00:05:29,495 --> 00:05:31,622
It's hard when your partner's family

108
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:34,000
are all hoodlums.

109
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:36,169
Then blood gets spilled in their family.

110
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:37,336
That's a big no-no.

111
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:43,134
[sighs] I just want Atoy
to have his own family.

112
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:47,430
You know, miss, sometimes Atoy and I

113
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:50,975
seem cursed in things like this.

114
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:52,101
- Single?
- [quirky sting]

115
00:05:52,935 --> 00:05:54,562
- It's hard to be handsome.
- [quirky sting]

116
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,314
That's our "handsome problems".

117
00:05:56,397 --> 00:05:58,399
Sometimes the world just isn't fair.

118
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,026
[Ame] Oh.

119
00:06:00,777 --> 00:06:03,237
It's hot outside, but it's windy here.

120
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:05,364
Signal number three!

121
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:06,908
Doesn't seem like it.

122
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:11,245
Ame, weren't you with Atoy
when you took Ibyang to school?

123
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,997
Has he arrived at the tailoring shop?

124
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:14,791
Oh, he hasn't.

125
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:17,126
The thing is, Miss Cita,

126
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:20,213
Atoy wanted to see Janine,

127
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:24,342
but he found out Janine
was already pulled out from school.

128
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:27,887
It looks like Audrey is avoiding
a meeting between father and daughter.

129
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:30,681
So, where is Atoy now?

130
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,142
Oh, no.

131
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:35,061
[pensive music playing]

132
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:37,355
I think I know.

133
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:39,273
I think I know where Atoy is.

134
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:48,533
Sir, they're not here,

135
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:50,159
so please don't cause a scene.

136
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:51,369
- [Emerson] Boss, wait.
- [indistinct]

137
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,037
- My companion. Hold on.
- [indistinct]

138
00:06:53,121 --> 00:06:55,248
She's not at her house,
and I know this is where she'd come.

139
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:57,792
So, call your master, bring Audrey out.

140
00:06:57,875 --> 00:06:58,835
- [Emerson] Wait, wait, wait.
- [Atoy] Audrey!

141
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:00,711
Wait, wait, brother. Atoy, Atoy!

142
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,923
Hold on. Ah. Calm down first.
Sir, I'll handle this.

143
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:05,550
- I'll handle him.
- Call her!

144
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:07,051
- [Emerson] Sorry, yes.
- Call her.

145
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:09,846
- Okay. I'll handle it.
- No, call her. Surely she's there!

146
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:12,432
'Toy, 'Toy, calm down first.

147
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:15,309
Leave Audrey alone for now.
Maybe she just needs space.

148
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,562
Of course, you still want her, but…

149
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:20,481
maybe she's just thinking
about her next move.

150
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,608
You shouldn't have stormed here.

151
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:24,402
Aren't you nervous
about what you're doing?

152
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:26,779
I'm not doing anything.
I just want to talk. That's all.

153
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:29,157
- Hey, Gavin!
- [in English] Bro Atoy, you should leave.

154
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,075
Gavin, talk to your Aunt Audrey.

155
00:07:31,826 --> 00:07:34,120
Tell her, if she doesn't
want to talk to me,

156
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:35,705
she shouldn't involve Janine.

157
00:07:36,372 --> 00:07:38,833
I've been calling her. She won't answer.

158
00:07:38,916 --> 00:07:41,502
Tell her to talk to me properly.

159
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:44,338
[music fades]

160
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:46,048
Why? What's so funny?

161
00:07:46,632 --> 00:07:49,218
You have the nerve
to order me around, huh?

162
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,012
[in English] After what you did
to my family?

163
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:52,847
I thought you were kind!

164
00:07:54,515 --> 00:08:01,314
I'm not kind,
especially to murderers like your father.

165
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:03,691
You have no evidence!

166
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,194
I know my father's reputation!

167
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:08,154
[in English] But he doesn't deserve
what you did to him,

168
00:08:08,237 --> 00:08:09,655
and especially to my grandfather!

169
00:08:10,239 --> 00:08:12,116
You know, I pity you.

170
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,994
I know you're a good kid.

171
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:18,289
You're just surrounded by liars.

172
00:08:18,372 --> 00:08:20,124
[pensive music playing]

173
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,459
You're the pitiful one!

174
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:23,169
There are more liars around you!

175
00:08:23,252 --> 00:08:24,462
Why don't you ask Karla?!

176
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:26,422
What?

177
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:28,132
Who?

178
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,092
- [Gavin] No one.
- Karla?!

179
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:31,928
- No-- No one.
- [Atoy] What do you mean, no one?

180
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,597
What about Karla? Huh, Gavin?

181
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:35,848
[tense music playing]

182
00:08:35,932 --> 00:08:38,017
- Uh--
- What about Karla?!

183
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:41,062
[music swells, fades]

184
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,231
Is Atoy there?

185
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,733
Just ignore him.

186
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:48,152
He'll leave soon.

187
00:08:58,287 --> 00:09:03,501
[pensive music playing]

188
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:09,966
Mommy, are you okay?

189
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,099
Janine, child.

190
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:22,436
Is it okay with you

191
00:09:23,437 --> 00:09:25,982
not to be with your daddy for now?

192
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:29,777
I was thinking,

193
00:09:30,903 --> 00:09:34,907
once we get clearance
from your grandfather's doctor…

194
00:09:38,327 --> 00:09:39,704
I want us

195
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:42,123
to go to the States.

196
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:45,334
We're going to America?

197
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:49,046
I want that, Mommy. I want to see snow!

198
00:09:50,089 --> 00:09:53,759
Is it okay with you not to see
your daddy anymore?

199
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:57,597
It's okay. He's bad anyway.

200
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,390
He hurt Grandpa.

201
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:04,186
[melancholic music playing]

202
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:11,736
- What were you saying about Karla?! Gavin!
- [dramatic sting]

203
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,195
- [Emerson] Enough, enough, enough.
- [Gavin] Nothing, nothing.

204
00:10:13,279 --> 00:10:14,322
No, you were saying something!

205
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:15,615
- [Emerson] Enough, 'Toy.
- What is it?!

206
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,033
- Gavin, enough, enough.
- Gavin, what about Karla--

207
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,451
Sir, just relax. [groaning]

208
00:10:18,534 --> 00:10:19,994
Huh? Gavin!

209
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:22,330
Gavin!

210
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,124
- Gavin!
- [Emerson mutters]

211
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:26,542
‪-[muttering]
‪-[groaning]

212
00:10:28,461 --> 00:10:30,338
No. It's fine now. It's fine.

213
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:32,923
It's fine, sir. Okay, it's fine.
It's okay. We'll handle it.

214
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,175
I'll take care of it.

215
00:10:34,258 --> 00:10:36,427
[tense music playing]

216
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:39,263
'Toy, let's go. Come on.

217
00:10:39,347 --> 00:10:40,222
Let's go.

218
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:43,059
[in English] So, Dad, you're just gonna
let Atoy get away with everything?

219
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,769
He shot you!

220
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:46,729
Our men died and were hurt.

221
00:10:46,812 --> 00:10:49,732
[in English] He's entitled
to that rage, Martina.

222
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:53,152
He didn't mean to shoot me.

223
00:10:55,696 --> 00:11:00,242
That damned husband of yours pulled me,
that's why I got shot!

224
00:11:01,202 --> 00:11:03,287
Dad, you don't need to say that.

225
00:11:03,371 --> 00:11:04,997
[in English] You're being unfair to Red.

226
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:07,875
It's all his fault anyway.

227
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:12,963
From that hit-and-run
to what happened to me.

228
00:11:13,881 --> 00:11:16,634
[in English] He's stupid and a coward!

229
00:11:17,635 --> 00:11:19,887
[suspicious music playing]

230
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:22,598
I want to file a case,

231
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,351
but then there'll be an investigation,

232
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:29,063
and the details
of what he did will come out.

233
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:38,739
Dad, did Audrey ask you?

234
00:11:41,492 --> 00:11:42,993
[in English] It was my decision.

235
00:11:43,619 --> 00:11:45,704
I just made it seem to Audrey

236
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:47,998
that Atoy intentionally shot me,

237
00:11:48,666 --> 00:11:50,209
so she'd get angry at him

238
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:52,837
and leave that man.

239
00:11:56,257 --> 00:11:58,175
Isn't that what you wanted?

240
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:00,886
If Red was the only reason,

241
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:03,639
Audrey wouldn't leave Atoy.

242
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:06,684
[music fades]

243
00:12:07,852 --> 00:12:12,481
Nurse, what room
is Red Regalia confined in?

244
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:13,774
I'll get back to you, sir.

245
00:12:13,858 --> 00:12:15,484
Wait a moment. Excuse me.

246
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:17,862
[phone ringing]

247
00:12:17,945 --> 00:12:18,988
[grunts]

248
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:24,743
Roger, what's the news?

249
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:27,663
I found the nun Boss Red was looking for.

250
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:29,748
She's with her niece.

251
00:12:32,793 --> 00:12:34,378
[Mongki on the phone] <i>I'll let you know.</i>

252
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:37,631
You can't talk to Boss Red yet.

253
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:41,760
Just don't take your eyes off them.

254
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:43,053
Understand?

255
00:12:43,137 --> 00:12:44,096
Copy.

256
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:47,308
Brother, will it take long?

257
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:51,645
- [man] Ah, Ma'am, here it is.
- [Faye] Oh. Oh, here. Thank you!

258
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,982
Auntie Norma, our order is here.

259
00:12:56,400 --> 00:12:57,985
[Norma] Hmm! Thank you.

260
00:12:58,068 --> 00:13:01,197
Auntie, Doc's secretary texted me.

261
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:05,868
Looks like Doc will be late,
so we can arrive around 6 p.m. instead.

262
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:09,205
[mutters]

263
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:12,917
[stammers] Did-- Did you get

264
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,253
Ame's number?

265
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:20,132
Ah, not yet.
Her coworker hasn't texted me.

266
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:24,595
But she told me yesterday
she'd ask their coworkers.

267
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:28,599
Who else are you looking for, besides Ame?

268
00:13:30,684 --> 00:13:31,852
[mutters]

269
00:13:31,936 --> 00:13:34,396
- [stammers] It's--
- [niece] It's…

270
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:37,608
A-- A…

271
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:41,237
to-- toy.

272
00:13:41,820 --> 00:13:43,614
Sorry.

273
00:13:43,697 --> 00:13:45,741
I pretended to be a nun.

274
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:49,745
This was the only way I could talk to you.

275
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:55,960
[in English] Sister…

276
00:13:57,628 --> 00:14:01,257
[in English] Ivy Santos, eight years old.

277
00:14:01,924 --> 00:14:03,384
We call her Ibyang.

278
00:14:04,426 --> 00:14:06,095
She's a good kid, but…

279
00:14:06,178 --> 00:14:08,055
a bit mischievous and cheeky.

280
00:14:08,138 --> 00:14:09,515
But still kind.

281
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:11,850
I'm sending her to school.

282
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:13,811
Atoy?!

283
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:16,939
Ah. Do you know Atoy's full name?

284
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:19,191
Maybe I can find him on the Internet.

285
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:28,075
[stammers] Or-- even A--Ame.

286
00:14:28,158 --> 00:14:31,287
Be-- because…

287
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:36,959
she's the one…

288
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,921
who will lead…

289
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:44,091
us-- to A-- Atoy

290
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:46,135
and Ib--yang.

291
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:54,435
[music fades]

292
00:14:55,227 --> 00:14:57,563
Emerson, watch over Atoy, okay?

293
00:14:57,646 --> 00:15:00,691
And don't go back to the Regalia house.

294
00:15:00,774 --> 00:15:02,234
Okay. Be careful.

295
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:03,193
[in English] Bye.

296
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,237
How's Atoy?

297
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:07,948
[sighs]

298
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:10,868
Audrey didn't face Atoy.

299
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:14,163
He almost fought with Red's son, Gavin.

300
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:16,999
[sighs] Unbelievable.

301
00:15:17,082 --> 00:15:20,210
Atoy really needs a vacation.
You and Ibyang should go with him, okay?

302
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:22,004
Yes. I'm game for that.

303
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:24,006
Want a snack?

304
00:15:24,089 --> 00:15:25,174
- Sure.
- I'll get some.

305
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,592
[grunts softly]

306
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:30,888
I'm really game for that.

307
00:15:30,971 --> 00:15:33,390
Especially now that things are unclear
between Audrey and Atoy.

308
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:37,937
[phone ringing]

309
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:42,775
Hello? Who is this?

310
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:44,401
Ms. Ame?

311
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:46,070
I got your number from Ms. Grace,

312
00:15:46,153 --> 00:15:48,822
your former coworker at Home of Tomorrow.

313
00:15:49,406 --> 00:15:52,785
I'm Sister Norma's niece.
We're here in Manila!

314
00:15:53,452 --> 00:15:54,870
Sister Norma is alive?

315
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,164
Yes. She just arrived last week.

316
00:15:57,247 --> 00:16:01,502
She wants to talk to you
about Ibyang's parents.

317
00:16:01,585 --> 00:16:03,629
Can we meet later?

318
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:06,548
Ah, yes-- Okay. Where can we meet you?

319
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:07,800
[tense music playing]

320
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:10,052
Why didn't he have him jailed?

321
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:12,096
What the hell? Was he hypnotized by Atoy?

322
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:13,931
[in English] Dad has his reason.

323
00:16:14,014 --> 00:16:15,557
And don't contradict him.

324
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:16,976
You're already being blamed
for everything.

325
00:16:17,059 --> 00:16:18,060
Of course.

326
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:20,854
[scoffs] I'm always at fault.

327
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:23,065
He'd probably be happier if I were dead.

328
00:16:23,857 --> 00:16:26,360
[in English] Hon,
he was protecting you from Atoy.

329
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:28,904
It's better he's not in jail.

330
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:31,240
It's easier for me to get revenge outside.

331
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:32,783
Oh, and then?

332
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:35,244
If you do that, Dad will be even angrier.

333
00:16:35,327 --> 00:16:37,413
[in English] Even if Dad
doesn't like Atoy,

334
00:16:37,496 --> 00:16:38,956
he's tied to Audrey.

335
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,958
You know how strong
Audrey's influence is on Dad.

336
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:42,418
That's another problem.

337
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:45,754
I need to think of a way
to get back at him.

338
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,674
That bastard always gets lucky.

339
00:16:48,757 --> 00:16:50,259
[anxious music playing]

340
00:16:50,342 --> 00:16:52,886
Don't think about that now, okay?

341
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:56,140
The day will come
when you'll have Atoy by the neck.

342
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:04,314
[phone ringing]

343
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:06,692
Now you're calling me.

344
00:17:06,775 --> 00:17:08,193
Tsk! Whatever.

345
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:12,656
If it's two, it's straight--

346
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,741
- straight through.
- Oop, oop, oop.

347
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:15,242
Oh, there. Karla!

348
00:17:15,325 --> 00:17:16,452
Karla, look.

349
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:17,619
Help me, Karla!

350
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,538
- It's fine, it's fine…
- Emerson!

351
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,498
- [Emerson] Sit here. Stay here.
- [Atoy groans]

352
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:23,167
- [Cita] What the hell?!
- [groans]

353
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:24,752
- Didn't I say, stay with him?
- [Emerson chuckles]

354
00:17:24,835 --> 00:17:26,837
Why did you bring him home drunk?!

355
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:28,881
I did stay with him!

356
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,299
I stayed to drink with him!

357
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:32,926
He invited me, of course.

358
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:33,844
Miss, come on.

359
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:35,095
How could I not go with him?

360
00:17:35,179 --> 00:17:40,559
Better than him hanging out again
outside Audrey's house.

361
00:17:40,642 --> 00:17:41,977
- Yes.
- [Cita mutters]

362
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:42,936
[Cita] Stay with him.

363
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,688
I'll get a towel.

364
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:46,231
[Emerson giggles]

365
00:17:46,315 --> 00:17:47,483
[groans]

366
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,068
- [Emerson] Wa-Wait, I'll go to the CR.
- Oh my!

367
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:51,028
- [Emerson] CR. Where's the CR?
- Go ahead.

368
00:17:51,111 --> 00:17:52,696
[Emerson coughing]

369
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:56,784
Drinking doesn't suit you. What's this?

370
00:17:57,743 --> 00:17:59,203
Pull yourself together!

371
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:02,915
- [pensive music playing]
- [inhales]

372
00:18:02,998 --> 00:18:04,124
[Atoy grunts]

373
00:18:04,208 --> 00:18:05,250
[Atoy] Hey, Karla.

374
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:06,376
‪[inhales]

375
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:08,587
‪[exhales]

376
00:18:12,549 --> 00:18:14,635
Gavin told me something.

377
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:22,559
He said you're a liar.

378
00:18:23,769 --> 00:18:26,313
[sinister music playing]

379
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:29,066
Are you hiding something from me?

380
00:18:38,492 --> 00:18:40,035
Brother, I don't know about that.

381
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:42,204
Nothing.

382
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:47,209
[music fades]

383
00:18:49,419 --> 00:18:52,923
[melancholic music playing]

384
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:01,682
Karla, I've known you
since you were a child.

385
00:19:05,018 --> 00:19:06,937
I know when you're lying.

386
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:10,983
I see it in your eyes.

387
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:12,067
There.

388
00:19:14,820 --> 00:19:17,197
I feel it in your pulse.

389
00:19:21,368 --> 00:19:22,536
So?

390
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:27,457
Do you have something to tell me?

391
00:19:31,211 --> 00:19:32,754
- [in English] Brother, I'm sorry.
- Hmm?

392
00:19:32,838 --> 00:19:34,464
Is there something I should know?

393
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:38,010
Or something you need to admit…

394
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:40,470
Why would he call you a liar?

395
00:19:41,096 --> 00:19:42,806
- Brother, I don't know how!
- Huh?

396
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:43,932
[Atoy] Huh? How?

397
00:19:45,767 --> 00:19:47,769
I just hope you won't be angry with us.

398
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,022
Angry?

399
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:53,775
[Karla] I hope you won't be angry with us.

400
00:19:53,859 --> 00:19:55,068
Karla!

401
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:56,945
Why would I be angry with you?

402
00:19:57,571 --> 00:19:59,907
Let your Brother Atoy rest.

403
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,783
- Emerson!
- Godmother, what is she saying?

404
00:20:01,867 --> 00:20:05,454
Emerson! Take Atoy upstairs
so he can lie down properly. Go on!

405
00:20:05,537 --> 00:20:07,331
- [Atoy] Godmother, Karla!
- [Cita] Take him upstairs.

406
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,415
[Emerson] Yes.

407
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:10,459
[Atoy] W-Why--

408
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:13,962
Wow.

409
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,548
That's a lot.

410
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:19,426
[Emerson humming]

411
00:20:19,509 --> 00:20:20,886
[sighs]

412
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:23,263
- [music fades]
- [Emerson chuckles]

413
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,350
[Emerson] So many.

414
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:29,061
- [suspicious music playing]
- [Emerson belches]

415
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:52,542
[Cita] Karla, what was that?

416
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,836
Are you going to tell Atoy the truth?

417
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:56,838
Didn't I warn you?

418
00:20:56,922 --> 00:20:59,424
Mom, it seems Brother Atoy
already knows something.

419
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,385
It should come from us, Mom.

420
00:21:01,468 --> 00:21:02,511
No, Karla.

421
00:21:02,594 --> 00:21:05,514
We won't add more
to what he's going through.

422
00:21:08,183 --> 00:21:10,102
How do you know he knows?

423
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:12,771
Did you tell anyone else?

424
00:21:15,983 --> 00:21:17,192
No, Mom.

425
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:20,779
He just brought it up now.

426
00:21:20,862 --> 00:21:22,489
How would he have an idea

427
00:21:22,572 --> 00:21:24,074
if no one told him?

428
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:27,369
[tense music playing]

429
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,414
So, your real father

430
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,040
is Brother Atoy's father?

431
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:34,251
[in English] That makes him
your half-brother.

432
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:37,462
[pensive music playing]

433
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:43,468
[barker] <i>Baclara, Baclaran, Baclaran!</i>
<i>Baclaran! Baclaran!</i>

434
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:46,179
[barker] Baclaran, Baclaran, Baclaran!

435
00:21:46,263 --> 00:21:48,432
[Atoy] Ma, are you with Dad too?

436
00:21:49,099 --> 00:21:50,225
[Julie on the phone] <i>No.</i>

437
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:51,518
<i>He'll be home later.</i>

438
00:21:51,601 --> 00:21:54,271
<i>He said he's meeting a client outside.</i>

439
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:56,815
Ah, is that so?

440
00:21:57,733 --> 00:21:59,359
[pensive music playing]

441
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:00,736
[sighs]

442
00:22:01,486 --> 00:22:03,238
O-Okay, Ma.

443
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:04,823
I'll-- I'll head home too.

444
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:22,549
[suspicious music playing]

445
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:32,893
[Emerson] Mmm?

446
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:51,495
[Emerson] Hey, 'Toy.

447
00:22:54,748 --> 00:22:59,336
Don't touch Miss Cita's bag.
Go upstairs to your room.

448
00:22:59,419 --> 00:23:01,004
Go on. I have somewhere to go too.

449
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:04,549
Hmm, I'll just go with you, Sir Delfin.

450
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:13,016
You're good at buying, huh?

451
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:15,102
[young Karla] <i>Dad!</i>

452
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,686
<i>My hair!</i>

453
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:19,106
[Delfin] Come on, hurry.

454
00:23:26,363 --> 00:23:28,907
[epic music playing]

455
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:45,132
Godmother.

456
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:49,553
I'm sorry, Karla.

457
00:23:49,636 --> 00:23:51,221
I know you're struggling,

458
00:23:51,304 --> 00:23:53,598
but he shouldn't know the truth.

459
00:23:53,682 --> 00:23:54,850
[melodramatic music playing]

460
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:57,936
Mom, isn't it better
if he learns the truth from us?

461
00:23:59,437 --> 00:24:01,690
Rather than figuring it out himself?

462
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:12,576
Godmother.

463
00:24:35,432 --> 00:24:36,850
Is this yours?

464
00:24:38,852 --> 00:24:40,478
Yes, Atoy.

465
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:43,481
[Cita titters]

466
00:24:51,531 --> 00:24:52,949
Atoy, why?

467
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:06,087
I'll never forget this scarf.

468
00:25:06,171 --> 00:25:08,840
[suspicious music playing]

469
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:10,884
Because I saw this.

470
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:12,636
[music fades]

471
00:25:12,719 --> 00:25:14,554
I saw this on

472
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:19,434
my father's mistress.

473
00:25:19,517 --> 00:25:20,852
[heavy music playing]

474
00:25:25,982 --> 00:25:27,108
[scoffs]

475
00:25:34,532 --> 00:25:37,869
Why, of all men, does it have to be
my father, Godmother?

476
00:25:37,953 --> 00:25:39,329
[sobs]

477
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:42,082
[music swells]

478
00:25:54,803 --> 00:25:56,554
I'll grow old single.

479
00:25:56,638 --> 00:25:58,515
I'm here, Master.

480
00:25:58,598 --> 00:26:01,935
Even if my parents take me,

481
00:26:02,811 --> 00:26:04,813
I'll still come to you.

482
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:08,566
All this time, Audrey's real child
has been right around us.

483
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:09,943
But we need to plan this.

484
00:26:10,026 --> 00:26:10,986
UP NEXT

485
00:26:11,069 --> 00:26:12,696
We need to get ahead of Atoy.

486
00:26:12,779 --> 00:26:14,906
It's risky. They're in the same house.

487
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:17,158
[Red] <i>He must not know</i>
<i>that Ibyang is his child.</i>

488
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:19,035
[Mongki] <i>Don't do anything bad.</i>

489
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:20,745
- Brother.
- Or you'll go straight to the morgue.

490
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:23,373
[in English] Hello, Sister Norma.
Remember me?

491
00:26:23,456 --> 00:26:24,958
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

492
00:26:25,041 --> 00:26:28,461
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

493
00:26:28,545 --> 00:26:29,921
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

494
00:26:30,005 --> 00:26:31,506
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
